#. type: Title ##
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Background {#background}"
msgstr "Pangkalahatang-ideya {#background}"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"This tutorial demonstrates how to use a Multi-Product Formula (MPF) to achieve a lower Trotter error on our observable compared to the one incurred by the deepest Trotter circuit that we will actually execute.\n"
"MPFs reduce the Trotter error of Hamiltonian dynamics through a weighted combination of several circuit executions. Consider the task of finding observable expectation values for the quantum state\n"
"$\\rho(t)=e^{-i H t} \\rho(0) e^{i H t}$ with the Hamiltonian $H$. One can use Product Formulas (PFs) to approximate the time-evolution $e^{-i H t}$ by doing the following:\n"
msgstr ""
"Ipinapakita ng tutorial na ito kung paano gamitin ang isang Multi-Product Formula (MPF) upang makamit ang mas mababang Trotter error sa ating observable kumpara sa error na maidudulot ng pinakamalalim na Trotter circuit na ating isasagawa.\n"
"Binabawasan ng mga MPF ang Trotter error ng Hamiltonian dynamics sa pamamagitan ng may-timbang na kombinasyon ng ilang circuit execution. Isaalang-alang ang gawain ng paghahanap ng mga expectation value ng observable para sa quantum state\n"
"$\\rho(t)=e^{-i H t} \\rho(0) e^{i H t}$ na may Hamiltonian na $H$. Maaaring gumamit ng mga Product Formula (PF) upang tantiyahin ang time-evolution na $e^{-i H t}$ sa pamamagitan ng sumusunod:\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Write the Hamiltonian $H$ as $H=\\sum_{a=1}^d F_a,$ where $F_a$ are "
"Hermitian operators such that each corresponding unitary can be efficiently "
"implemented on a quantum device.\n"
msgstr ""
"Isulat ang Hamiltonian na $H$ bilang $H=\\sum_{a=1}^d F_a,$ kung saan ang "
"$F_a$ ay mga Hermitian operator na ang bawat katumbas na unitary ay maaaring"
" mahusay na maipatupad sa isang quantum device.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Approximate the terms $F_a$ that do not commute with each other.\n"
msgstr "Tantiyahin ang mga terminong $F_a$ na hindi nag-commute sa isa't isa.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Then, the first-order PF (Lie-Trotter formula) is:\n"
msgstr "Kaya naman, ang first-order PF (Lie-Trotter formula) ay:\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "$$S_1(t):=\\prod_{a=1}^d e^{-i F_a t},$$\n"
msgstr "$$S_1(t):=\\prod_{a=1}^d e^{-i F_a t},$$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"which has a quadratic error term $S_1(t)=e^{-i H "
"t}+\\mathcal{O}\\left(t^{2}\\right)$. One can also use higher-order PFs "
"(Lie-Trotter-Suzuki formulas), which converge faster, and are defined "
"recursively as:\n"
msgstr ""
"na may quadratic error term na $S_1(t)=e^{-i H "
"t}+\\mathcal{O}\\left(t^{2}\\right)$. Maaari ring gumamit ng higher-order PF"
" (Lie-Trotter-Suzuki formula), na mas mabilis na magkakalapit, at tinukoy "
"nang rekursibo bilang:\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "$$S_2(t):=\\prod_{a=1}^d e^{-i F_a t/2}\\prod_{a=1}^d e^{-i F_a t/2}$$\n"
msgstr "$$S_2(t):=\\prod_{a=1}^d e^{-i F_a t/2}\\prod_{a=1}^d e^{-i F_a t/2}$$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$S_{2 \\chi}(t):= S_{2 \\chi -2}(s_{\\chi}t)^2 S_{2 \\chi "
"-2}((1-4s_{\\chi})t)S_{2 \\chi -2}(s_{\\chi}t)^2,$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$S_{2 \\chi}(t):= S_{2 \\chi -2}(s_{\\chi}t)^2 S_{2 \\chi "
"-2}((1-4s_{\\chi})t)S_{2 \\chi -2}(s_{\\chi}t)^2,$$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"where $\\chi$ is the order of the symmetric PF and $s_p = \\left( 4 - "
"4^{1/(2p-1)} \\right)^{-1}$. For long time-evolutions, one can split the "
"time interval $t$ into $k$ intervals, called Trotter steps, of duration "
"$t/k$ and approximate the time-evolution in each interval with a $\\chi$ "
"order product formula $S_{\\chi}$. Thus, the PF of order $\\chi$ for time-"
"evolution operator over $k$ Trotter steps is:\n"
msgstr ""
"kung saan ang $\\chi$ ay ang order ng symmetric PF at $s_p = \\left( 4 - "
"4^{1/(2p-1)} \\right)^{-1}$. Para sa matagalang time-evolution, maaaring "
"hatiin ang time interval na $t$ sa $k$ na interval, na tinatawag na mga "
"Trotter step, na may tagal na $t/k$ at tantiyahin ang time-evolution sa "
"bawat interval gamit ang $\\chi$ order product formula na $S_{\\chi}$. Kaya "
"naman, ang PF ng order na $\\chi$ para sa time-evolution operator sa $k$ "
"Trotter step ay:\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$ S_{\\chi}^{k}(t) = \\left[ S_{\\chi} \\left( \\frac{t}{k} "
"\\right)\\right]^k = e^{-i H t}+O\\left(t \\left( \\frac{t}{k} "
"\\right)^{\\chi} \\right)$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$ S_{\\chi}^{k}(t) = \\left[ S_{\\chi} \\left( \\frac{t}{k} "
"\\right)\\right]^k = e^{-i H t}+O\\left(t \\left( \\frac{t}{k} "
"\\right)^{\\chi} \\right)$$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"where the error term decreases with the number of Trotter steps $k$ and the "
"order $\\chi$ of the PF.\n"
msgstr ""
"kung saan ang error term ay bumababa kasabay ng bilang ng mga Trotter step "
"na $k$ at ng order na $\\chi$ ng PF.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Given an integer $k \\geq 1$ and a product formula $S_{\\chi}(t)$, the "
"approximate time-evolved state $\\rho_k(t)$ can be obtained from $\\rho_0$ "
"by applying $k$ iterations of the product formula "
"$S_{\\chi}\\left(\\frac{t}{k}\\right)$.\n"
msgstr ""
"Kapag may ibinigay na integer na $k \\geq 1$ at isang product formula na "
"$S_{\\chi}(t)$, ang tinantyang time-evolved state na $\\rho_k(t)$ ay "
"maaaring makuha mula sa $\\rho_0$ sa pamamagitan ng pag-apply ng $k$ ulit ng"
" product formula na $S_{\\chi}\\left(\\frac{t}{k}\\right)$.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\rho_k(t)=S_{\\chi}\\left(\\frac{t}{k}\\right)^k \\rho_0 S_{\\chi}\\left(\\frac{t}{k}\\right)^{-k}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\rho_k(t)=S_{\\chi}\\left(\\frac{t}{k}\\right)^k \\rho_0 S_{\\chi}\\left(\\frac{t}{k}\\right)^{-k}\n"
"$$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$\\rho_k(t)$ is an approximation for $\\rho(t)$ with the Trotter "
"approximation error ||$\\rho_k(t)-\\rho(t) ||$. If we consider a linear "
"combination of Trotter approximations of $\\rho(t)$:\n"
msgstr ""
"Ang $\\rho_k(t)$ ay isang tantiya para sa $\\rho(t)$ na may Trotter "
"approximation error na ||$\\rho_k(t)-\\rho(t) ||$. Kung isasaalang-alang "
"natin ang isang linear na kombinasyon ng mga Trotter approximation ng "
"$\\rho(t)$:\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\mu(t) = \\sum_{j}^{l} x_j \\rho^{k_j}_{j}\\left(\\frac{t}{k_j}\\right) + \\text{some remaining Trotter error} \\, ,\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\mu(t) = \\sum_{j}^{l} x_j \\rho^{k_j}_{j}\\left(\\frac{t}{k_j}\\right) + \\text{some remaining Trotter error} \\, ,\n"
"$$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"where $x_j$ are our weighting coefficients, $\\rho^{k_j}_j$ is the density matrix corresponding to the pure state obtained by evolving the initial state with the product formula, $S^{k_j}_{\\chi}$, involving $k_j$ Trotter steps, and $j \\in {1, ..., l}$ indexes the number of PFs that make up the MPF. All the terms in $\\mu(t)$ use the same product formula $S_{\\chi}(t)$ as its base.\n"
"The goal is to improve upon ||$\\rho_k(t)-\\rho(t) \\|$ by finding $\\mu(t)$ with even lower $\\|\\mu(t)-\\rho(t)\\|$.\n"
msgstr ""
"kung saan ang $x_j$ ay ang ating mga weighting coefficient, ang $\\rho^{k_j}_j$ ay ang density matrix na katumbas ng pure state na nakuha sa pamamagitan ng pag-evolve ng initial state gamit ang product formula, $S^{k_j}_{\\chi}$, na nagsasangkot ng $k_j$ Trotter step, at ang $j \\in {1, ..., l}$ ay nag-i-index ng bilang ng mga PF na bumubuo sa MPF. Lahat ng termino sa $\\mu(t)$ ay gumagamit ng parehong product formula na $S_{\\chi}(t)$ bilang basehan.\n"
"Ang layunin ay mapabuti ang ||$\\rho_k(t)-\\rho(t) \\|$ sa pamamagitan ng paghahanap ng $\\mu(t)$ na may mas mababang $\\|\\mu(t)-\\rho(t)\\|$.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$\\mu(t)$ needs not be a physical state as $x_i$ need not be positive. The "
"goal here is to minimize the error in the expectation value of the "
"observables and not to find a physical replacement for $\\rho(t)$.\n"
msgstr ""
"Hindi kailangang maging pisikal na estado ang $\\mu(t)$ dahil hindi "
"kailangang positibo ang $x_i$. Ang layunin dito ay mabawasan ang error sa "
"expectation value ng mga observable at hindi upang makahanap ng pisikal na "
"kapalit para sa $\\rho(t)$.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$k_j$ determines both the circuit depth and level of Trotter approximation. "
"Smaller values of $k_j$ lead to shorter circuits, which incur fewer circuit "
"errors but will be a less accurate approximation to the desired state.\n"
msgstr ""
"Tinutukoy ng $k_j$ ang parehong circuit depth at antas ng Trotter "
"approximation. Ang mas maliit na halaga ng $k_j$ ay nagbubunga ng mas "
"maikling mga circuit, na nagdudulot ng mas kaunting circuit error ngunit "
"magiging mas hindi tumpak na tantiya ng nais na estado.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The key here is that the remaining Trotter error given by $\\mu(t)$ is "
"smaller than the Trotter error that one would obtain by simply using the "
"largest $k_j$ value.\n"
msgstr ""
"Ang susi dito ay ang natitirang Trotter error na ibinibigay ng $\\mu(t)$ ay "
"mas maliit kaysa sa Trotter error na makukuha kung gagamitin lamang ang "
"pinakamataas na halaga ng $k_j$.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "You can view the usefulness of this from two perspectives:\n"
msgstr ""
"Maaaring tingnan ang kapaki-pakinabang nito mula sa dalawang perspektibo:\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '1. '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"For a fixed budget of Trotter steps that you can execute, you can obtain "
"results with a Trotter error that is smaller in total.\n"
msgstr ""
"Para sa isang nakapirming badyet ng Trotter step na maisasagawa, makakakuha "
"ng mga resulta na may mas maliit na Trotter error sa kabuuan.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '2. '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Given some target number of Trotter steps that is too large to execute, you "
"can use the MPF to find a collection of lower-depth circuits to run that "
"results in a similar Trotter error.\n"
msgstr ""
"Kung may target na bilang ng Trotter step na masyadong malaki upang "
"maisagawa, maaaring gamitin ang MPF upang makahanap ng isang koleksyon ng "
"mas mababang-lalim na mga circuit na nagbubunga ng katulad na Trotter "
"error.\n"

